{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. As you're all aware, we have 1,200 cast aluminum housings on hold due to cosmetic residue from the forming operation. Before I can make any decision on authorizing rework and releasing the campaign plan, we need to go through our standard pre-authorization review. I'd like to hear from process engineering, maintenance, quality, and EHS so we can assess whether the ultrasonic cleaning cell is ready for this rework and confirm we have the documented inspection process lined up for release. Let's start with process engineering -- can you walk us through the current state of the residue issue and what rework approach you're proposing?"}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to share an important finding from a process trial I completed yesterday. I tested the residue removal on the housings, and the results show that the residue can be successfully removed from only 900 of the 1,200 housings using our ultrasonic cleaning process. The remaining 300 housings have embedded residue that cannot be removed by this method, and they will have to remain on hold. I have not yet entered this result into the production release system, but I'm disclosing it now so it's factored into the decision."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "I need to share an important update from the customer side. This morning I received a revised plan from the customer portal, and I confirmed in the customer control plan that every reworked housing must receive dimensional scanning. Additionally, the plan requires exactly 30 reworked housings to be retained for customer review. I have not yet updated our local inspection instruction to reflect these requirements, so we need to account for both the dimensional scanning capacity and the retention of 30 units when we plan this rework campaign."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "I need to share an important finding from my waste review. I determined that the spent cleaning solution from this campaign must be collected in exactly 2 sealed waste totes and shipped under a waste manifest. I confirmed the classification with our site's waste contractor this week, but I have not yet updated the area waste-board notice. We'll need to ensure those 2 totes are staged and the manifest is prepared before the rework campaign begins."}
```

